segment.content:
The title of the 1980 ethnographic film directed by John Marshall in collaboration with Adrienne (likely Adrienne LaFrance, a noted collaborator in anthropological film) about the !Kung people, whose footage was reused in *The Gods Must Be Crazy* (1980), is **Nǃai, the Story of a ǃKung Woman**.

This film, first broadcast in 1980 as part of the PBS *Odyssey* series, is documented in the search results as containing footage that was later incorporated into *The Gods Must Be Crazy*. The film provides an intimate portrait of Nǃai (a Juǀʼhoansi woman) and her community, aligning with the description of a 1980 ethnographic film focused on the !Kung people.

\boxed{Nǃai, the Story of a ǃKung Woman}

